      "nets": ["/Microcontroller/NET0016", "Net-(D6-K)", "GND", "Net-(J5-Pin_2)"],
      "observed": "The only heater-related status LED/resistor pair is D6/R10 on the MCU control net /Microcontroller/NET0016, which is driven by ESP32 GPIO1 and also connected to U4 IN/DIAG_EN. The actual heater output net from U4 OUT to the heater screw terminal J5 pin 2 has no LED or series resistor connected to it.",
      "expected": "The specification states that a status LED and series resistor are on the HEATER output net, so that the LED visually indicates the actual energized heater output. In the netlist this would require the LED/resistor to be connected to Net-(J5-Pin_2), not to the GPIO1 control net.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "A status LED (`D2`) and series resistor (`R3`) are also on the `HEATER` net, so the heater output doubles as a visual \"heater on\" indicator at the board level"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"6\") (name \"/Microcontroller/NET0016\") ... (node (ref \"D6\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") ... (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"GPIO1/ADC1_CH1/XTAL_32K_N\") ... (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"IN\") ... (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"DIAG_EN\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"17\") (name \"Net-(D6-K)\") (node (ref \"D6\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"K\") (node (ref \"R10\") (pin \"1\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"23\") (name \"Net-(J5-Pin_2)\") (node (ref \"J5\") (pin \"2\") (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"OUT\")"}
      ],
      "impact": "The board LED will light whenever GPIO1 is asserted, even if the TPS1H200 high-side switch is faulted, disabled, or the heater output is not actually energized. This changes the intended behavior from an output-state indicator to a command-state indicator.",
      "confidence": 0.58
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most power, SPI, thermocouple, fan, USB, and high-side switch connectivity matches the specification despite reference-designator changes. The main functional deviation is that the heater status LED/resistor appears to be connected to the MCU heater-control net rather than the actual switched heater output net."
}

